course: dictionary
lesson: 13010
title: A rare, strong word: extirpate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Extirpate is a formal word. It means to destroy something completely, pulling it out by the roots so that none is left.
explain: Look at the clues around it: «Wolves were extirpated from Britain long ago, but they still live in Canada.» The words «but they still live» tell you the wolves are gone from Britain, not from the whole world. Extirpate is about one place.
explain: Try a swap. «The villagers wanted to ___ the rats from their barns.» Does destroy completely fit? Yes, so extirpate means something close to that.
fact: Extirpate means to destroy something completely, or to remove it totally.
fact: You can extirpate animals, diseases, ideas or crimes. The word is always about getting rid of something all the way.
fact: When a species is extirpated from an area, it has died out there but may still live somewhere else.
fact: In medicine, to extirpate means to remove an organ or growth completely by surgery.
fact: Extirpate is a rare, formal word, so you will mostly meet it in books, news and science writing.
exercise: «Wolves were extirpated from Britain long ago, but they still live in Canada.» What does extirpated mean here? | Fed and looked after by people | Moved to a new country on holiday | Made bigger and stronger | *Died out in that area
exercise: «The villagers worked hard to extirpate the rats from their barns.» What does extirpate mean? | To paint brightly | To count carefully | *To destroy completely, so none are left | To feed and look after
exercise: Which word means about the same as extirpate? | *Eradicate | Celebrate | Decorate | Hesitate
test: «The doctor had to extirpate the small growth by surgery.» What does the doctor do? | Shows it to the class | Covers it with a bandage | Measures it with a ruler | *Removes it completely with an operation
test: «Bears were extirpated from many places, yet some still live in the mountains.» What does this show? | They were all brought back | *They died out in those places but still live elsewhere | They became bigger and stronger | They moved to the mountains because they liked them
exam: «The team hoped to extirpate the disease from the region.» Which best explains the sentence? | Hoping to paint the region in bright colours | Hoping to make the disease spread faster | *Hoping to destroy the disease completely in that area | Hoping to forget that the disease ever existed
